# SoC Integration

## Goal

The goal of this project is to integrate the hardware components developed throughout the previous projects into one complete System-on-Chip (SoC) architecture.

Up to this point, the individual components have been developed and tested separately.

The purpose of this project is to connect them together and create a functioning hardware system.

The SoC will contain:

- CPU
- ROM
- RAM
- Register File
- ALU
- UART
- GPIO
- Timer
- Interrupt Controller
- Memory-Mapped I/O
- Wishbone Bus

The final architecture should look approximately like:

    ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │                     SoC                       │
    │                                               │
    │                 ┌──────────┐                  │
    │                 │  RISC-V  │                  │
    │                 │   CPU    │                  │
    │                 └────┬─────┘                  │
    │                      │                        │
    │                Wishbone Bus                   │
    │                      │                        │
    │          ┌───────────┼────────┐               │
    │          │           │        │               │
    │          ▼           ▼        ▼               │
    │         ROM         RAM      MMIO             │ 
    │                               │               │
    │                  ┌────────────┼──────────┐    │
    │                  │            │          │    │
    │                  ▼            ▼          ▼    │
    │                 UART         GPIO      Timer  │
    │                                               │
    │                     Timer IRQ                 │
    │                         │                     │
    │                         ▼                     │
    │                Interrupt Controller           │
    │                         │                     │
    │                         ▼                     │
    │                        CPU                    │
    │                                               │
    └───────────────────────────────────────────────┘

This project is the final integration step before moving into the Linux preparation stage.

---

## What is a SoC?

SoC stands for System-on-Chip.

A SoC combines multiple components required for a computer into one integrated hardware system.

Instead of having:

    CPU
    RAM
    UART
    GPIO
    Timer
    Interrupt Controller

as completely separate systems, they are connected together into one architecture.

For this project, the FPGA will contain the complete SoC.

Conceptually:

    FPGA
      │
      ▼
    SoC
      │
      ├── CPU
      ├── Memory
      ├── Peripherals
      ├── Bus
      └── Interrupt System

---

## Why This Project?

The previous projects focused on individual components.

For example:

    ALU
    RAM
    ROM
    Register File
    UART
    GPIO
    Timer
    Interrupt Controller

These components are useful individually, but they do not form a computer until they are connected together.

This project answers the question:

- How do all these components communicate to form a computer?

The main concepts are:

- Bus communication
- Address decoding
- Memory-mapped peripherals
- CPU and memory interaction
- CPU and peripheral interaction
- Interrupts
- System-level integration

